{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3170","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3170","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3170\",\"parent_revision\":\"e100d0d5e9cfb6745491f4b212321c1abbbe05ab\",\"root_revision\":\"88517ee18bcc3b6121fdb7f2cbbadb6501acdf1872db2e6cbe0b271d7cf71aff\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3168 fixed doc-drift-auditor and rewrite-room-auditor, which were instructed to write a generated audit report to a fixed filename in the repository root or under .claude/reports/. That is how one run's output became committed content (plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md).\\n\\nThe same pattern remains in other plugins and was left out of that PR because it is a multi-plugin design decision, not a one-line fix:\\n\\nNon-gitignored destinations (generated output would become committed content in whatever repo the plugin is installed into):\\n- plugins/plugin-creator/agents/plugin-assessor.md \u2014 writes the assessment report to .plugin-creator/reports/plugin-assessment-{plugin-name}.md\\n- plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-skill-lifecycle/SKILL.md and plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md \u2014 write audit artifacts to .plugin-creator/audits/\\n- .plugin-creator/ is not gitignored in this repo. Note that plugin-creator uses .plugin-creator/ as a coherent workspace convention (reports, audits, plans), and refactor-executor and refactor-validator read plans back out of it \u2014 so the fix is a decision about whether that whole directory should be gitignored, not a per-agent path edit.\\n\\nDestinations under .claude/, which trigger a permission prompt for the user and are prohibited for agent output:\\n- plugins/holistic-linting/skills/holistic-linting/SKILL.md, its references/pre-existing-issues-protocol.md, and skills/holistic-linting-orchestrator/SKILL.md \u2014 resolution and architectural-review reports in .claude/reports/\\n- plugins/python3-development/skills/stinkysnake/SKILL.md and plugins/python-engineering/skills/stinkysnake/SKILL.md \u2014 static-analysis, type-inventory, plan-review and doc-update reports in .claude/reports/\\n- plugins/python3-development/skills/stinkysnake/references/agent-prompts.md and plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/agent-prompts.md \u2014 plan-review reports in .claude/reports/\\n- .claude/skills/delegate/SKILL.md \u2014 the delegation template's own worked example instructs writing findings to .claude/reports/NAME-YYYYMMDD.md, so it teaches the prohibited path to every agent that reads it\\n\\nThe delegate skill example is the highest-leverage one: it is the pattern every other delegation copies.\\n\\nImpact: an agent following any of these leaves a generated report behind at a path a consumer will commit, or triggers a permission prompt mid-run. The established convention already used by dh:dispatch, plugin-creator's skill-auditor, and skill-content-updater is .tmp/scratch/reports/ plus returning the path.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **generated agent reports still route to committed or permission-prompted paths across plugins** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Found while removing committed doc-drift-auditor output (PR #3168)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a71db876542ae4a865fdb38fea495711a5b3ce3765744bbdcbf51396e5c341dd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQOMknw\"}"}